-- B-2.2-b1 / ARCH B-2 (#1113): THE `keyForSite` NO-ROW ARM, WHICH IS THE ARM
-- `b1` MUST NOT BREAK.
--
-- `fillImplDefaults` is SAME-MODULE ONLY, so a method-less impl declared in a
-- module OTHER than the interface's carries an empty method list.  `keyForSite`'s
-- candidate scan requires method-name membership, so it never sees this impl and
-- answers `None`, and the caller's `fromOption tag (...)` supplies the bare head
-- tag `Box`.  That tag is not a hedge over a selector result: it is the ONLY
-- source of the `<TAG>` in the emitter's `@mdk_default_<method>_<TAG>` symbol
-- (`llvm_emit.emitDefaultRKey`, reached after `implFor` misses and
-- `emitGeneralRKey` misses).  A `b1` that deleted `fromOption tag` -- which every
-- design document before RUN-P3-013 said it would -- breaks EVERY cross-module
-- default-inheritance call site in the tree, and this fixture is the pin for it.
--
-- HAND-DERIVED FROM THE SPEC, not captured: both impls are method-less, so both
-- occurrences run the interface default `sz _ = 42`.  100 * 42 + 42 = 4242.
-- EXPECTED: 4242
--
-- ⚠️ THE VALUE IS NOT THE ASSERTION.  Both arms answer 42, so the value cannot
-- tell the two dispatch paths apart -- and an exit-code-graded control cannot
-- either: this shape exits 0 today and would still exit 0 with a WRONG symbol,
-- right up until the link fails.  The discrimination lives in this gate's
-- Section 3 rows, which pin BOTH emitted symbols by name:
--   * `@mdk_default_sz_Box`  -- the cross-module (no-row) arm, keyed on the tag
--     `fromOption tag` supplies;
--   * `@mdk_impl_Cup_sz`     -- the same-module twin, whose specialized clause
--     makes it an ordinary tagged impl.
-- Their COEXISTENCE in one program is the point: one source shape, two routes,
-- and only the pair shows that `b1` moved neither.
import iface.{Sz(..), sz, Cup(..)}

data Box = Box

impl Sz Box where

main = println (sz Box * 100 + sz Cup)
